</ul>

<!-- Why Insulated Drylining -->
<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Why Choose Insulated Drylining?</h2>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li><strong>Significantly warmer rooms:</strong> Insulated drylining raises the internal surface temperature of cold walls, reducing condensation and making rooms feel more comfortable during colder months.</li>
  <li><strong>Lower heating costs:</strong> By reducing heat loss through external walls, insulated drylining can lower your heating bills and reduce your carbon footprint.</li>
  <li><strong>Scottish Building Standards compliant:</strong> Our insulated drylining installations meet the thermal performance requirements of Scottish Building Standards Section 3 (Energy) and Part L of the Building Regulations.</li>
  <li><strong>Improved moisture control:</strong> Properly designed insulated drylining includes vapour control layers and moisture management to prevent hidden condensation and mould problems — critical for Edinburgh's older properties.</li>
  <li><strong>Faster than external wall insulation:</strong> Internal insulated drylining is quicker to install than external wall insulation and does not require external works or planning permission in most cases.</li>
  <li><strong>Suitable for all property types:</strong> Whether you have a solid wall Victorian tenement in the New Town, a modern new build in New Craigmillar, or a commercial property in Leith, we can design an insulated drylining system that delivers the performance you need.</li>
</ul>

